        "title": "Nanofabrication: Top-Down Lithography and Bottom-Up Deposition",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Nanofabrication is the set of processes that create structures at 1-100 nm. Top-down\nmethods start with bulk material and remove or pattern it. Bottom-up methods build\nfrom atoms and molecules. Production semiconductor manufacturing is almost entirely\ntop-down; emerging nanotechnology uses both."
